WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.516
Search engines and social networks read a few values from every page:

00:00:05.516 --> 00:00:08.767
its title, a description, and a preview picture.

00:00:08.767 --> 00:00:14.006
The SEO module lets you set defaults for the whole site and values for each page.

00:00:14.006 --> 00:00:15.210
Let's see how.

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:23.007
The SEO module keeps these values in two places.

00:00:23.007 --> 00:00:27.685
Social Meta Settings holds defaults for the whole site, and they apply to

00:00:27.685 --> 00:00:31.830
every page that shows a content item, whatever its content type.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:36.081
The SeoMeta part holds the values of a single page.

00:00:36.081 --> 00:00:40.381
You attach it to a content type, such as Article, and its fields

00:00:40.381 --> 00:00:42.899
appear in an SEO tab of the editor.

00:00:42.899 --> 00:00:46.400
A value set on the page wins over the site default.

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:52.597
Open Graph and Twitter Card are two formats that describe how a shared link is presented.

00:00:52.597 --> 00:00:56.382
The module has a panel for each, and both can start from the

00:00:56.382 --> 00:00:58.790
same title, description and picture.

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:09.430
The SEO module is a feature, so let's start in Tools, Features, and search for SEO.

00:01:09.958 --> 00:01:12.362
Select Enable on the SEO feature.

00:01:12.362 --> 00:01:17.478
Orchard Core also enables any feature that SEO depends on, and a notification

00:01:17.478 --> 00:01:19.698
confirms that SEO was enabled.

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:26.592
Open Settings, then Social Meta Settings.

00:01:26.592 --> 00:01:30.401
These fields hold the defaults that a page uses when it has no

00:01:30.401 --> 00:01:31.690
value of its own.

00:01:32.174 --> 00:01:36.719
Default Meta Description is the summary for pages without a Meta Description.

00:01:36.719 --> 00:01:39.184
Let's type one sentence about the site.

00:01:39.647 --> 00:01:43.340
The same page also has defaults for Open Graph and Twitter, such as

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:48.400
Open Graph Type, Default Open Graph Description, Twitter Card and Default Twitter Description.

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:49.867
Let's leave them empty.

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:52.845
The Social card holds the pictures.

00:01:52.845 --> 00:01:57.956
Default social image is the picture for shared links, unless Open graph image

00:01:57.956 --> 00:02:00.912
or Twitter Image sets a more specific one.

00:02:00.912 --> 00:02:04.360
Select Add media, choose a picture, and select OK.

00:02:04.823 --> 00:02:07.804
Select Media text and describe the picture.

00:02:07.804 --> 00:02:12.001
The module uses this text as the alternative text of the image.

00:02:12.001 --> 00:02:17.353
Select Save, and the message Site settings updated successfully confirms the save.

00:02:21.563 --> 00:02:24.300
Page values come from the SeoMeta part.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:29.533
Let's open Design, Content Definition, Content Types, and edit the Article type.

00:02:29.995 --> 00:02:31.523
Select Add Parts.

00:02:31.523 --> 00:02:34.912
SeoMeta is in the list, with its description.

00:02:34.912 --> 00:02:40.295
Select Add & Configure on its row to attach the part and open its settings.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:46.376
Five checkboxes, each starting with Display, decide which panels the editor shows:

00:02:46.376 --> 00:02:50.971
Keywords, Custom Meta Tags, Open Graph, Twitter and Google Schema.

00:02:50.971 --> 00:02:52.950
All five start unchecked.

00:02:53.412 --> 00:02:58.448
Let's check Display Open Graph and Display Twitter, and leave the others off.

00:02:58.448 --> 00:03:02.392
Select Save, and a notification confirms the part settings.

00:03:06.607 --> 00:03:10.852
Let's open Content, Content Items, and edit the About article.

00:03:10.852 --> 00:03:13.599
The editor has a second tab named SEO.

00:03:13.599 --> 00:03:14.597
Select it.

00:03:15.053 --> 00:03:17.082
Render is checked by default.

00:03:17.082 --> 00:03:21.603
When you clear it, the SEO module writes no values for this page at all.

00:03:22.058 --> 00:03:26.084
Page Title overrides the title that the browser shows for the page.

00:03:26.084 --> 00:03:29.228
Its hint recommends keeping it under 70 characters.

00:03:29.228 --> 00:03:30.938
Let's type a short title.

00:03:31.401 --> 00:03:34.486
Meta Description is a short summary of the page.

00:03:34.486 --> 00:03:36.201
Let's type one sentence.

00:03:36.664 --> 00:03:40.685
Canonical overrides the address that identifies the page.

00:03:40.685 --> 00:03:44.770
It stays empty, so the module uses the page's own address.

00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:49.430
Meta Robots, the robots meta tag of this page, stays empty too, and

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:53.514
a separate video covers the robots file of the whole site.

00:03:53.974 --> 00:04:00.068
In the Social card, Default social image sets one picture for both Open Graph and Twitter.

00:04:00.068 --> 00:04:03.624
Select Add media, choose a picture, and select OK.

00:04:04.116 --> 00:04:06.809
Select Media text and describe the picture.

00:04:06.809 --> 00:04:10.766
This text becomes the alternative text of the image for this page.

00:04:11.248 --> 00:04:16.050
The Open Graph and Twitter cards have their own title and description fields.

00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:20.678
Here they stay empty, so they use the Page Title and the Meta Description.

00:04:21.131 --> 00:04:22.411
Select Publish.

00:04:22.411 --> 00:04:25.153
The content of the page stays as it is.

00:04:25.153 --> 00:04:30.273
The module adds these values behind the page, for browsers, search engines and

00:04:30.273 --> 00:04:32.101
social networks to read.

00:04:36.301 --> 00:04:38.037
Each value has an order.

00:04:38.037 --> 00:04:42.494
The Page Title replaces the whole browser title, without the site name.

00:04:42.494 --> 00:04:47.877
Meta Description comes from the page, then from Default Meta Description, and Canonical

00:04:47.877 --> 00:04:51.061
from the page, then from the address of the page.

00:04:51.811 --> 00:04:55.926
For sharing, a title comes from its own field, the Page Title, then

00:04:55.926 --> 00:04:57.673
the content item's title.

00:04:57.673 --> 00:05:02.576
A description comes from its own field, the page's Meta Description, then Default

00:05:02.576 --> 00:05:07.311
Open Graph Description or Default Twitter Description in Social Meta Settings.

00:05:08.061 --> 00:05:10.014
Pictures follow four steps:

00:05:10.014 --> 00:05:14.572
the specific picture of the page, the Default social image of the page,

00:05:14.572 --> 00:05:19.367
the specific picture in Social Meta Settings, and its Default social image.

00:05:19.367 --> 00:05:24.161
The media text, which becomes the alternative text, follows the same order.

00:05:26.161 --> 00:05:30.320
Set the defaults once in Social Meta Settings, and add the SeoMeta part

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:33.777
to the content types whose pages need values of their own.

00:05:33.777 --> 00:05:35.181
Thanks for watching.

